    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-04T22:48:03+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T22:48:03+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T13:18:03Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T13:18:03Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough lies near the western border ahead of a cold front moving across the Bight, while a weak ridge of high pressure lies across central Australia. The front and trough will move across SA overnight and into southeastern Australia on Saturday, with a ridge of high pressure developing across SA in its wake. A trough is expected to develop near the western border on Sunday and remain near stationary nearly next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-04T22:46:13+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T13:16:13Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Coober Pedy. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower east of Stuart Highway in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Woomera in the early morning. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h turning east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 27.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 3:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-07T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-06T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of fog south of Woomera in the early morning. Medium chance of showers in the far west in the late afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning then tending east to southeasterly in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-07T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-08T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-06T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-07T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds easterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-08T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-09T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-07T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-08T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds easterly 20 to 30 km/h turning southeasterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 25.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
